ct joint\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t271 pop up button (collapsed, settable) Description: Comparison graph joint, Value: Joint 2, Secondary Actions: Expand\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t272 menu\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t273 Joint 1\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t274 (selected) Joint 2\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t275 Joint 3\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t276 Joint 4\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t277 Joint 5\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t278 Joint 6\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t279 Joint 7\n+\t\t\t\t\t280 text Signed torque · shared Nm scale Selected · sampled peak -3.154  Nm at  6.132  s\n+\t\t\t\t\t281 container Joint 2: selected signed peak -3.154 Nm at 6.132 seconds; reference signed peak -1.186 Nm at 4.566 seconds. Largest absolute sampled values, aligned by window start, shared Nm scale.\n+\t\t\t\t\t282 text Reference · sampled peak -1.186  Nm at  4.566  s 0 ms Time from each window’s start 1024  ms Circles mark each curve’s largest absolute sampled torque, with its signed value.  Raw samples.  Peaks are measurements, not detected collisions. Motion phases may differ.\n+\t\t\t\t283 button (collapsed) All 7 joint measurements, Secondary Actions: Expand\n+\t\t\t\t\t284 text All 7 joint measurements\n+\t\t\t\t285 container\n+\t\t\t\t\t286 text Joint 2  variability:  0.322  →  0.626  Nm. Mean shift:  +0.541  Nm.\n+\t\t\t\t287 heading What to check next, Value: 3\n+\t\t\t\t\t288 text What to check next\n+\t\t\t\t289 container\n+\t\t\t\t\t290 text Inspect  Joint 2  in both windows. Confirm the motion phase, payload and intended contact were comparable before attributing the change to a fault.\n+\t\t\t\t291 button Inspect selected signal\n+\t\t\t\t\t292 text Inspect selected signal\n+\t\t\t\t\t293 image\n+\t\t\t\t294 heading How to verify a change, Value: 3\n+\t\t\t\t\t295 text How to verify a change\n+\t\t\t\t296 text After an engineer chooses an adjustment, compare a matched window from the new recording. Lower variation alone does not prove a repair worked or the robot is safe.\n+\t\t\t\t297 button (collapsed) Method & source windows, Secondary Actions: Expand\n+\t\t\t